        "mission_intent": "We're planning a major migration of our legacy case management platform to a cloud-native microservices architecture, and I need the engineering team to develop a comprehensive security specification that covers the full migration lifecycle aligned with NIST SP 800-64 Rev. 2 guidance on technology advancement and major system migrations. The spec must address the tendency we've seen in past projects where baseline security requirements get relaxed or waived to accelerate deployment timelines \u2014 I want explicit controls preventing that from happening this time. The specification should account for risks of reintroducing known vulnerabilities through flawed integration practices, especially given that we're combining several legacy data feeds with new API-based services, which compounds our exposure surface. I need the team to apply best efforts to ensure zero security regressions throughout the migration while also meeting our aggressive go-live target of March 31st, even though the full security assessment and ATO process for the new environment typically takes five to six months and we're only starting now. Please also include enrollment and disenrollment procedures for the new environment, address selective technology obsolescence risks, and ensure synergy across the old and new platforms doesn't introduce compounding security gaps. Route the draft spec to me and the ISSO for review by end of next week.",
